<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78704" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παράρρῡμα</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παράρῡμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρύω</span> A)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>anything drawn along</i>
			or <i>over something</i> : </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>leathern</i> or <i>hair curtain, stretched along</i> the
			sides of ships to protect the men, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				1.6.19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.1629.451
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1668.86
			</span></i>, al., Moschioap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				5.208c
			</span></i> (Casaubon for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρατρήματα</span>),
				<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				35.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ποδός</span>
			<i>covering</i> for the foot, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				527
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> pl., of
				<i>fasteners</i> for bandages, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18(2).748
			</span></i> (nisi leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραρραμμάτων</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
